---
source: crates/accelbyte-ags-cli/tests/snapshot/help_text.rs
expression: stdout
---
Print the current access token to stdout

  Prints a secret. The token is written to stdout on its own, with
  nothing else, so a script can reuse this session instead of running
  its own login:

    curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $(ags auth token)" ...

  The token is resolved exactly as an API call resolves it:
  AGS_ACCESS_TOKEN first, then the stored token, refreshing it when
  it has expired. Exits 2 with login guidance when authentication
  fails, or 4 when the identity service cannot be reached. Stdout is
  empty in both cases.

  --dry-run is refused because the command's only output would be a
  live credential.

  Redirect stdout with care: anything that captures it captures a
  live credential.

  With --format json, outputs the token alongside its expiry and
  source.

Usage:
  auth token

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
